DTSTAMP:20260924T115707Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250318
SUMMARY:Arizona: 165 (partnership) / 120S (S-corp) due
DESCRIPTION:Arizona partnership return due the 15th day of the 3rd month af
 ter year-end. AZ's PTE elective tax is filed with the same Form 165/120S. C
 orrection (this rebuild session): the cited source states the general rule 
 (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026-specific weekend in
 teraction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with every other state 
 in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shift policy (e.g. Mass
 achusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oregon all confirm sh
 ifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universal US government-dead
 line convention of shifting to the next business day\, this entry's date_20
 26 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This
  is a computed application of the general shift convention\, not an indepen
 dently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this specific state's statute
  shifts - flagged here for transparency. | Arizona partnership return due t
 he 15th day of the 3rd month after year-end. AZ's PTE elective tax is filed
  with the same Form 165/120S. File Arizona Form 120/165EXT by the original 
 due date\, or rely on a valid federal extension for the same period. Full t
 ax\, penalties\, and interest remain due by the original due date regardles
 s of extension. Correction (this rebuild session): the cited source states 
 the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026-sp
 ecific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with e
 very other state in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shift 
 policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oreg
 on all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universal U
 S government-deadline convention of shifting to the next business day\, thi
 s entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to Marc
 h 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the general shift convention
 \, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this specifi
 c state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | Authority: Ariz
 ona Department of Revenue\, direct fetch this session: "a partnership whose
  taxable year ends on December 31st must file its partnership return by Mar
 ch 15th of the following year" and "All partnership returns are due on or b
 efore the 15th day of the third month following the close of the partnershi
 p's taxable year." | Source: https://azdor.gov/sites/default/files/document
 /FORMS_PARTNERSHIP_2025_165_i.pdf | This date is computed from a recurrence
  rule and may not reflect a later-announced change\; confirm against the ci
 ted source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
